WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:07.520
The code we have seen so far to work with files&nbsp;
is efficient but can sometimes seem cumbersome.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.320
We can consolidate the amount of code we have&nbsp;
to write using the with statement, which opens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:18.160
a file, performs an action on a file, and then&nbsp;
closes that file without having to tell Python to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:24.280
close the file. Having a file close ensures that&nbsp;
the memory space the file uses will be recovered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:30.240
thus helping a device run more efficiently and&nbsp;
reducing the chance of data corruption. In this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.880
318-with code file, we have the same first four&nbsp;
lines of code as we did for the video on writing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:45.640
to a file. Starting on line 6, I am going to&nbsp;
rewrite this code, using the with keyword, and you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:57.240
will see the difference in the code efficiency. I&nbsp;
will type with, copy the open statement from line&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:18.920
1 to here, add the words as message, and then a&nbsp;
colon. I will make sure the next line is indented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:24.600
as with is a block of code, and then I will copy&nbsp;
the two write statements to lines 7 and 8 and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:49.520
ensure both are indented. Then, I will comment&nbsp;
out the code on lines 1 through 4. On line 9,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.520 --> 00:02:05.649
I will add a print statement to tell us the file&nbsp;
has been created. Then I will run this code,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.649 --> 00:02:09.640
and the file has been created. The file management&nbsp;
section is complete, so it is time for a code&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:19.760
analysis exercise. This 318-analysis file has the&nbsp;
same code we just worked on, with one addition:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:27.120
a print statement to read the code on line 10.&nbsp;
Use the Review 3.1 exercise in the workbook to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:35.280
answer questions on this code. In the next video,&nbsp;
we will discuss the answers to those questions.

